module Core

# ============================================================================
# DecimalTrig — sine, cosine and tangent of D32, D64 and D128.
# A decimal argument x = c * 10^e is reduced modulo pi/2 EXACTLY from its coefficient and exponent: the
# fraction of a turn x / (2 pi) comes from an integer multiply by a tabled 512-bit fraction, so no
# rounding of x to binary happens before the reduction. (Rounding a large x to B128 first, as the older
# code did, moved it by up to x * 2^-113, which is a different angle once x is large, and near a multiple
# of pi even a small x lost most of its relative accuracy.) The reduced angle |t| <= pi/4 then goes to the
# correctly rounded B128 sin/cos for D32 and D64 (the result is kept only when its error bound cannot move
# the decimal rounding, else the W=192 engine recomputes it) and to the W=192 engine for D128.
# ============================================================================

### frac(10^a / (2 pi)) for a = 32 * i, i = 0..190 (every decimal128 exponent up to 6111 is 32 * i + b,
### b < 32), as 512-bit binary fractions, eight U64 words per entry, the high word first (truncated).
